index 83fe99db..b25cae85 100644
--- a/docker/npu_patch/README.md
+++ b/docker/npu_patch/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,25 @@
 
 This guide provides instructions for installing Vime with NPU support, including the required dependencies and patches.
 
+Sparse HCCL is selected with `--update-weight-mode delta
+--update-weight-transport sparse_hccl --update-weight-delta-verify-every 0`.
+Install both dependency patches together: VIME's first update calls
+`send_dense_weight_chunk` and sends values only, then later updates use
+checkpoint-coordinate sparse patches. Every inference worker receives the full
+chunk before PP filtering. Values replace positions; they are not additive deltas.
+
+The dependency patches retain VIME extensions beyond the upstream sparse HCCL
+wrapper: dense bootstrap, PP handling, batched sender validation and optional
+Qwen3-MoE BF16/ND direct writes (`VIME_SPARSE_MOE_DIRECT=1`, default disabled).
+Unmatched direct-write layouts fall back to native loading. Quantized/NZ weights
+and EPLB are unsupported. ETP>1 and additional model families require validation.
+Sparse updates are in-place: a failure after transmission starts requires
+reconnection and a new dense seed before reuse.
+
+The receiver compares sparse bounds in int64 even when wire indices are int32,
+so valid coordinates in checkpoint tensors with at least `2**31` elements are
+not rejected by scalar overflow. This does not extend the int32 wire range.
+
